-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Online Codes of Practice Procedure) Rules 2023 (S 47/2023), made under s 45L(2) of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-online-codes-of-practice-procedure-rules-2023/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S47-2023.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- These Rules bind the Authority's procedure for issuing, amending or revoking an online Code of Practice; for the person in the seat they are what the person may rely on:
-- a notice, a period of at least 28 days to object, and a duty on the Authority to consider objections made in time.

§ `Rule 2: Definitions`

-- src:7 | “contact address”, for a person, means any of the following nominated by the person for the receiving of documents under these Rules:
-- src:8 | ( a ) the person’s residential address in Singapore;
-- src:9 | ( b ) the person’s place of business or work in or outside Singapore;
-- src:10 | ( c ) an email address;
@ref rule 2(1) "contact address" (src:7-10)
GIVEN `it is the person's residential address in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the person's place of business or work in or outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an email address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person nominated it for the receiving of documents under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 2(1) the address is a contact address for the person` MEANS
    `the person nominated it for the receiving of documents under these Rules` AND (`it is the person's residential address in Singapore` OR `it is the person's place of business or work in or outside Singapore` OR `it is an email address`)

-- src:11 | “proposal” means a proposal by the Authority —
-- src:12 | ( a ) to issue an online Code of Practice, including issuing any online Code of Practice to replace another online Code of Practice; or
-- src:13 | ( b ) to amend or revoke an online Code of Practice.
@ref rule 2(1) "proposal" (src:11-13)
GIVEN `it is a proposal by the Authority to issue an online Code of Practice, including to replace another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a proposal by the Authority to amend or revoke an online Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 2(1) the thing is a proposal` MEANS
    `it is a proposal by the Authority to issue an online Code of Practice, including to replace another` OR `it is a proposal by the Authority to amend or revoke an online Code of Practice`

-- src:14 | (2) Where the time specified by these Rules for doing any act expires on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, the act is in time if done on the next following day that is neither a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.
@ref rule 2(2) (src:14)
-- The act is in time if done on the next following day that is neither a Saturday, Sunday nor public holiday.
GIVEN `the last day of the time specified falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is done on the next following day that is neither a Saturday, Sunday nor public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 2(2) the act done on that next day is in time` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the time specified falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday` THEN JUST `the act is done on the next following day that is neither a Saturday, Sunday nor public holiday` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Rules 3 to 6`

-- src:16 | 3. —(1) A proposal to issue an online Code of Practice, or to amend an online Code of Practice, must consist of —
-- src:17 | ( a ) a draft text of the proposed online Code of Practice to be issued (in replacement or otherwise), or the proposed amendment to an online Code of Practice, setting out —
-- src:18 | (i) a description of the online communication service or regulated online communication service (as the case may be), the providers of which the proposed online Code of Practice or amendment (as the case may be) is intended to apply to or to affect; and
-- src:19 | (ii) the provisions, specifications and particulars in relation to the proposal, and such other information and materials as are necessary to explain and illustrate the proposal; and
-- src:20 | ( b ) any other relevant reports or documents.
@ref rule 3(1) (src:16-20)
GIVEN `it has a draft text of the proposed online Code of Practice or amendment, describing the services whose providers it is intended to apply to or affect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the draft sets out the provisions, specifications and particulars and the other information and materials necessary to explain and illustrate the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has any other relevant reports or documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 3(1) the proposal to issue or amend consists of what the rule requires` MEANS
    `it has a draft text of the proposed online Code of Practice or amendment, describing the services whose providers it is intended to apply to or affect`
    AND `the draft sets out the provisions, specifications and particulars and the other information and materials necessary to explain and illustrate the proposal`
    AND `it has any other relevant reports or documents`

-- src:21 | (2) A proposal to revoke an online Code of Practice must —
-- src:22 | ( a ) identify the online Code of Practice to be revoked; and
-- src:23 | ( b ) consist of such information and materials as are necessary to explain and illustrate the proposal.
@ref rule 3(2) (src:21-23)
GIVEN `it identifies the online Code of Practice to be revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it consists of the information and materials necessary to explain and illustrate the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 3(2) the proposal to revoke consists of what the rule requires` MEANS
    `it identifies the online Code of Practice to be revoked` AND `it consists of the information and materials necessary to explain and illustrate the proposal`

-- src:25 | 4. —(1) The Authority must, after notifying the Minister of its proposal —
-- src:26 | ( a ) give notice to the general public of the making of the proposal on https://www.imda.gov.sg/regulations-and-licences/Regulations/consultations; and
-- src:27 | ( b ) give notice of the proposal to —
-- src:28 | (i) the providers of any online communication service or regulated online communication service (as the case may be), the providers of which the proposed online Code of Practice or amendment (as the case may be) is intended to apply to or to affect; or
-- src:29 | (ii) the general public in any manner that will secure adequate publicity for the proposal.
@ref rule 4(1) (src:25-29)
GIVEN `the Authority notified the Minister of its proposal first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave notice to the general public on the Authority's consultations web page` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave notice to the providers of the services concerned, or to the general public in a manner that secures adequate publicity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 4(1) the Authority has given the notices the rule requires` MEANS
    `the Authority notified the Minister of its proposal first` AND `the Authority gave notice to the general public on the Authority's consultations web page` AND `the Authority gave notice to the providers of the services concerned, or to the general public in a manner that secures adequate publicity`

-- src:30 | (2) The notice required by paragraph (1)( b ) to be given must —
-- src:31 | ( a ) state that the Authority has prepared a draft text of the proposed online Code of Practice to be issued, or the proposed amendment to an online Code of Practice, or of the revoking of an online Code of Practice, in the proposal; and
-- src:32 | ( b ) invite persons to whom the notice is given to give written objections to and representations about the proposal covered by the notice to the Authority at an address and within a specified period in accordance with paragraph (3).
@ref rule 4(2) (src:30-32)
GIVEN `the notice states that the Authority has prepared a draft text or the revoking of an online Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice invites written objections and representations to the Authority at an address and within a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 4(2) the notice says what the rule requires` MEANS
    `the notice states that the Authority has prepared a draft text or the revoking of an online Code of Practice` AND `the notice invites written objections and representations to the Authority at an address and within a specified period`

-- src:33 | (3) The period within which objections to and representations concerning a proposal covered by a notice required by paragraph (1)( b ) must be a period of not less than 28 days after the notice is given.
@ref rule 4(3) (src:33)
GIVEN `the days after the notice is given that the period allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 4(3) the period for objections and representations is long enough` MEANS
    `the days after the notice is given that the period allows` AT LEAST 28

-- src:35 | 5. —(1) Any objection to or representation concerning a proposal must —
-- src:36 | ( a ) be in writing and in English;
-- src:37 | ( b ) be given to the Authority —
-- src:38 | (i) at the address stated in the notice given under rule 4(1)( b ); and
-- src:39 | (ii) within the period specified in the notice in accordance with rule 4(3); and
-- src:40 | ( c ) be accompanied by a statement of the reasons or explanations for the objection or representation, and the contact address of the person making the objection or representation.
@ref rule 5(1) (src:35-40)
GIVEN `the objection or representation is in writing and in English` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given to the Authority at the address stated in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given within the period specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accompanied by a statement of the reasons or explanations and the contact address of the person making it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 5(1) the objection or representation is as the rule requires` MEANS
    `the objection or representation is in writing and in English` AND `it is given to the Authority at the address stated in the notice` AND `it is given within the period specified in the notice` AND `it is accompanied by a statement of the reasons or explanations and the contact address of the person making it`

-- src:41 | (2) The Authority may refuse any objection to or representation concerning a proposal that —
-- src:42 | ( a ) is given to the Authority after the expiry of the time limit for the giving of the objection or representation imposed by these Rules; or
-- src:43 | ( b ) is incomplete or otherwise not made in accordance with these Rules.
@ref rule 5(2) (src:41-43)
GIVEN `it is given after the expiry of the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is incomplete or otherwise not made in accordance with these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 5(2) the Authority may refuse the objection or representation` MEANS
    `it is given after the expiry of the time limit` OR `it is incomplete or otherwise not made in accordance with these Rules`

-- src:44 | (3) The Authority is under no duty to hold in‑person hearings and may decide an objection to or representation concerning a proposal without an in‑person hearing.
@ref rule 5(3) (src:44)
GIVEN `the Authority decides the objection or representation without an in-person hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 5(3) the Authority is under a duty to hold an in-person hearing` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:46 | 6. —(1) Except where the Authority is of the opinion that an objection or representation is of a frivolous nature, the Authority must consider every objection or representation to a proposal which has been received by it within the period specified in accordance with rule 4(3) and which has not been withdrawn.
@ref rule 6(1) (src:46)
GIVEN `the Authority is of the opinion that the objection or representation is of a frivolous nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was received within the period and has not been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 6(1) the Authority must consider the objection or representation` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority is of the opinion that the objection or representation is of a frivolous nature`) AND `it was received within the period and has not been withdrawn`

-- src:47 | (2) After so considering the objections or representations to a proposal, the Authority may —
-- src:48 | ( a ) issue an online Code of Practice, with such modifications as the Authority may consider necessary;
-- src:49 | ( b ) amend or revoke an online Code of Practice, with such modifications as the Authority may consider necessary; or
-- src:50 | ( c ) withdraw the proposal in whole or in part, and then give a notice to the general public as soon as practicable and in any manner that will secure adequate publicity for the making of that decision.
@ref rule 6(2) (src:47-50)
GIVEN `the Authority has considered the objections or representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 47/2023 rule 6(2) the Authority may issue, amend or revoke an online Code of Practice with modifications it considers necessary, or withdraw the proposal in whole or in part` MEANS
    `the Authority has considered the objections or representations`
